first_seen_date\":\"2025-11-01\",\"risk_score\":23,\"risk_history\":[{\"date\":\"2025-12-01\",\"event\":\"onboarding_review\",\"decision\":\"approve\",\"note\":\"Cleared after review; no action required.\"}]},{\"vendor_id\":\"V0050\",\"name\":\"Woodgrove Partners GmbH\",\"known_bank_accounts\":[\"WIRE-****2480\",\"ACH-****4580\",\"IBAN-DE**35****9962\"],\"historical_invoice_amounts\":[10255.71,13878.46,10459,11600.3,7373.21,9779.53,12887.76,6665.38],\"first_seen_date\":\"2026-03-13\",\"risk_score\":13,\"risk_history\":[]}]",
					"Step 2 - deterministic HOLD rule + amount analysis: use the Python tool to compute, from the extracted facts and the REAL vendor row, whether ALL THREE hold: (a) the invoice payee bank account is NOT in known_bank_accounts; (b) invoice amount > 2 * mean(historical_invoice_amounts); (c) (invoice_date - first_seen_date) < 30 days. If no vendor row was found, treat (a) and (c) as satisfied and the mean as unavailable. deterministic_hold = (a AND b AND c). Record which of a/b/c fired in rules_fired. Have the same Python call also return the invoice amount, the vendor historical mean, and their ratio for amount_analysis.",
					"Step 3 - risk assessment: from the invoice text and the facts, assess fraud indicators (missing or mismatched PO, urgency / same-day-wire language, bank-change language, round-sum amounts, amount outlier vs the vendor's own history, tax math that does not add up, inconsistent or missing dates, near-threshold amounts). Produce risk_score 0-100 and risk_level one of low|medium|high|critical, with a flags array.",
					"Step 4 - decision: queue_status = 'auto_hold' if deterministic_hold is true, or risk_level is critical with no vendor history; 'auto_cleared' if risk_level is low AND deterministic_hold is false AND both the vendor and the payee bank account are known; otherwise 'pending_review'.",
					"Step 5 - verification status: 'not_required' when queue_status is 'auto_cleared'; otherwise 'pending' (an out-of-band vendor verification runs asynchronously and is attached to this case later).",
					"Your ENTIRE reply is exactly one raw JSON object and nothing else: no report, no fraud-alert banner, no headings, no tables, no bullet points, no commentary, no code fences - before or after. The first character must be '{' and the last must be '}'. An optional top-level boolean \"unprocessable\" may be present (set by the Step 0 gate); omit it otherwise. Shape: { \"queue_status\": \"auto_cleared|pending_review|auto_hold\", \"invoice\": { \"invoice_number\": string, \"vendor_name\": string, \"amount\": string, \"currency\": string }, \"facts\": <the extracted+validated facts document, included verbatim>, \"amount_analysis\": { \"invoice_amount\": number, \"vendor_mean_amount\": number|null, \"ratio_vs_mean\": number|null, \"over_2x_mean\": boolean }, \"vendor\": { \"found\": boolean, \"vendor_id\": string|null, \"mean_amount\": number|null, \"bank_account_known\": boolean, \"amount_over_2x_mean\": boolean, \"days_since_first_seen\": number|null }, \"deterministic_hold\": boolean, \"rules_fired\": [string], \"risk\": { \"risk_score\": integer, \"risk_level\": \"low|medium|high|critical\", \"flags\": [ { \"type\": string, \"evidence\": string } ] }, \"verification\": { \"status\": \"not_required|pending\", \"result\": null }, \"summary\": string }."
				],
				"parameters": {}
			},
			"input": [
				{
					"lane": "questions",
					"from": "question_invoice"
				},
				{
					"lane": "documents",
					"from": "answer_documents_facts"
				}
			],
			"ui": {
				"position": {
					"x": 1620,
					"y": 300
				},
				"measured": {
					"width": 150,
					"height": 66
				}
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "agent_rocketride_1",
			"provider": "agent_rocketride",
			"config": {
				"agent_description": "AP invoice triage controller: vendor-master lookup + deterministic fraud rules + risk assessment, emits the full approval-queue case record.",
				"instructions": [
					"Follow the instructions carried in the incoming question exactly, including its Step 0 processability gate.",
					"FAST PATH (Step 0), check this before anything else: if no facts/context document is attached, or it is empty, or it has no non-empty vendor_name and no non-empty amount and no non-empty invoice_number, then do NOT enumerate or call any tool and do NOT narrate - your entire first-wave response must be exactly the 'unprocessable' JSON object specified in the question (starts with '{', ends with '}').",
					"Otherwise you have a real Python code-execution tool. Do Step 1 (vendor lookup) yourself by reading the VENDOR_MASTER JSON array carried in the question - do NOT call a tool for it. Then use the Python tool for real for the Step 2 deterministic rule + amount computation: do NOT emit tool-call syntax as text, do NOT write 'simulated result', and do NOT fabricate the computation output. For a processable invoice, a run whose Step 2 numbers did not come from a genuine Python tool call is invalid.",
					"Keep the real vendor row, the computed vendor mean, and the rule results in memory so the answer cites concrete values from actual tool output.",
					"CRITICAL OUTPUT RULE: your entire final answer is exactly one raw JSON object and nothing else. Do NOT prepend a markdown report, a fraud-alert banner, headings, tables, or any prose. Do NOT wrap the JSON in code fences. Your response must start with '{', end with '}', and be valid parseable JSON - a single object, never an array, never text plus JSON."
				],
				"max_waves": 8,
				"require_tool_call": false,
				"parameters": {}
			},
			"input": [
				{
					"lane": "questions",
					"from": "prompt_case"
				}
			],
			"ui": {
