		{
			"id": "prompt_verify",
			"provider": "prompt",
			"config": {
				"instructions": [
					"You simulate an out-of-band vendor verification call. PLACEHOLDER: this stands in for a future real telephony / voice integration (an outbound call or secure message to the vendor's on-file contact). Do not treat the simulated response as authoritative evidence.",
					"The question text is a JSON case that needs verification: it carries the invoice fields, the risk flags, and rules_fired. Generate 2-3 targeted verification questions derived from the specific flags (e.g. confirm the remittance bank account, confirm the PO number, confirm the invoice total and date). Simulate a plausible scripted vendor response to each question as a back-and-forth call between 'sentinel' (you) and 'vendor'. Judge the result 'confirmed' (responses are internally consistent and match the invoice) or 'suspicious' (evasive, inconsistent, or contradicts the invoice).",
					"The 'transcript' array is MANDATORY and must contain every turn of the simulated call in order, each as { \"speaker\": \"sentinel\"|\"vendor\", \"text\": string } - at minimum an opening sentinel line, one vendor reply per question, and a closing sentinel line. Never return an empty transcript. Put your reasoning/assessment in the 'notes' string, not in prose outside the object.",
					"Your ENTIRE reply is exactly one raw JSON object and nothing else: no report, no 'FRAUD ALERT' banner, no executive summary, no headings, no tables, no bullet points, no markdown, no commentary, no code fences (no ```), before or after. The first character must be '{' and the last must be '}'. Shape: { \"invoice_number\": string, \"verification\": \"confirmed|suspicious\", \"questions\": [string], \"transcript\": [ { \"speaker\": \"sentinel|vendor\", \"text\": string } ], \"notes\": string, \"completed_at\": string }."
				],
				"parameters": {}
			},
